POE2 Flask Helper @PROJECT_VERSION@
=======================

A tray application for Windows x64. It reads HP/Mana/Energy Shield/Ward/Rage from the
memory of Path of Exile 2 (PathOfExile.exe), and when a value drops below your
threshold it sends the flask key to the game as if you pressed it yourself. It never
writes to game memory.

The Russian version of this document is README.ru.txt.

Requirements
------------
Windows x64 and the Visual C++ v14 x64 Redistributable
(https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vc_redist.x64.exe). Nothing else is needed.

How to run
----------
Start POE2FlaskHelper.exe. The program lives entirely in the system tray and creates
no windows. On the first run it creates config.json next to the exe with default
settings: the archive does not contain config.json, your file is created by the
program, and an existing file is never overwritten. offsets.json is mandatory and
must be placed next to the exe: if it is missing, broken or incomplete, the program
shows a message and exits with code 2. An unknown option in config.json - a key the
program does not know, at any level (root, hotkeys, scanner, sound, vitals, a vital
name, logging) - makes the whole file invalid: on startup the program shows a
message, logs "config.json is invalid (unknown key \"...\")" and exits with code 2,
the same way as the missing offsets.json. Fix the key and start again.

Tray status (tooltip over the icon)
-----------------------------------
Line 1 is always "POE2FlaskHelper <version>"; the status follows on line 2:
  Scanner off          - module switched off, the game memory is not read at all;
  Waiting for game     - module on, the game process is not found yet;
  In menu / loading    - module on, the game process is open, the game is not in a zone
   (main menu, character selection, zone loading); the handle stays open, the scanner
   polls once a second and reads no values;
  Attached (PID n)     - module on, the game values are being read;
  Admin rights required - OpenProcess denied: the game is started as administrator, so
   the helper must be started with the same rights (see "Game run as administrator").
   The status disappears on the next poll that opens the game successfully.
When the hotkey is taken by another program the tooltip appends "hotkey Ctrl+9 busy";
the program keeps working, the tray menu remains available.

Controls
--------
Ctrl+9 - global hotkey, switches the scanner module on and off. It works while the
game has the focus. Enabling plays enable.wav, disabling plays disable.wav, at the
config sound.volume level (0 = silent).
Right-click the tray icon - a two-item menu:
  Enabled / Disabled - the switch; the text shows the current state, the checkmark
  marks the enabled module; clicking does the same as Ctrl+9.
  Exit - clean exit, the icon disappears from the tray.
Double-click on the icon does nothing.

Editing config.json at runtime
------------------------------
The program checks config.json every 5 seconds. Edit the file and save it: the settings
are validated and applied without a restart, the log gets a line
"config.json reloaded (sound.volume, vitals.Health.threshold)" listing the paths that
were applied, and reload.wav plays. Applied live: enabled / key / threshold / cooldownMs
of each Vital, scanner.pollIntervalMs, scanner.requireGameForeground,
scanner.processNames, sound.volume, hotkeys.toggleScanner (the hotkey is re-registered
and the tray tooltip updates), logging.level, logging.maxSizeKb, logging.keepFiles. A
live setting takes effect at the next scanner tick - at most 5 seconds + one poll after
the save. Saving the file without changes is a success too
("config.json reloaded (no changes)").
Two settings apply only after a restart and the log names them ("scanner.enabledOnStart
changed - applies after restart", "logging.file changed - applies after restart").
A broken config.json in runtime is an error line in the log, not a message box: the
program keeps running on the settings it has, the 5 s check continues, and the fixed file
is applied when you save it. An unknown key in runtime is handled the same way: the log
gets "config.json is invalid (unknown key \"<path>\"), current config kept", the
config is not applied at all, no sound plays, and the program keeps running on the
settings it already has - fix the key and save. If an editor holds the file with an
exclusive lock, or the file is deleted, you get one warning per check and the next
check tries again. If the new hotkey is taken by another program, the old one is kept
and the log warns.
No sound plays at startup: reload.wav plays only on a successful reload, at the
sound.volume level.

Files (everything lives next to the exe, the current directory is ignored)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
config.json  - settings, created by the program on the first run with defaults. It is
  not shipped in the archive and never overwritten by the program. scanner switch at
  start (enabledOnStart), poll interval, requireGameForeground, process names, the
  Ctrl+9 hotkey, sound volume (sound.volume, 0-100 % for enable.wav/disable.wav/
  reload.wav, 100 by default), and for each Vital: enabled, key, threshold (1-100 %),
  cooldownMs. The file is checked every 5 seconds (see "Editing config.json at
  runtime"): most settings apply on the fly, edit and save; enabledOnStart and
  logging.file apply after a restart. An unknown key makes the whole file invalid
  (see "How to run").
offsets.json - game offsets, mandatory. The first key "GameVersion" is the patch
  version string of the game (read by find_offsets.py from the game client log,
  e.g. "0.5.5f"); the program ignores it, it identifies the release archive. After a
  game patch the values stop matching and "Offsets mismatch" appears in the log. Fix:
  run find_offsets.py (python find_offsets.py --hp <HP> --mana <Mana> --es <ES>
  --current-hp <current HP> --tol 0 --save offsets.json, details in scanner/README.md)
  and put the new file next to the exe.
logs/app.log - UTF-8 log next to the exe, with rotation (logging.level,
  logging.maxSizeKb, logging.keepFiles in config.json). Start, exit, config warnings,
  hotkey registration, attach/detach, Offsets mismatch are written to the log. attach
  and detach are written once per game process, not once per poll: while the game is in
  the main menu / character selection / zone loading the log stays silent (status
  "In menu / loading", one line on entering it). Every
  flask key press is an info line ("Health 23% <= 50%, key=1"), and so is the single
  line of a cooldown window in which the value stayed below the threshold ("EnergyShield
  80% <= 80%, key=3 held: cooldown left 720 ms") - one such line per window, so you can
  see that the key was held back. The press line reads "<=" because the printed percent
  is rounded and a legal press can show a rounded percent equal to the threshold. The
  FIRST values line after attach and after entering the zone from the menu is an info
  line ("tick: Health ..."); every later tick stays debug-only: at logging.level = info
  the log has presses, held lines and that one first values line per attach/zone entry,
  no other value lines. The time zone lookup failure record (the log stamps fall back to
  UTC) is a debug line: it appears in the log only when logging.level is debug. At level
  debug, hovering the tray icon writes a burst of "tray callback event 512" lines
  (WM_MOUSEMOVE): normal noise, not a problem.

Game run as administrator
-------------------------
If the game is started as administrator, the helper must be started with the same
rights (right-click POE2FlaskHelper.exe -> Run as administrator). Otherwise Windows
UIPI blocks opening the game process and sending keys to it.
